/// MISCOMPILE — SILENT WRONG VALUE (2026-07-14, seed rcdzc, iter 41). A tree-walking interpreter over a
/// `Map String Int64` environment computes a SHADOWING `let` WRONG: evaluating an inner `let` that
/// re-binds a name `x` via `Map.insert(env, "x", …)` MUTATES the shared `env` in place, so a SIBLING read
/// of the OUTER `x` (in the same enclosing expression) sees the shadowed value instead of the outer one.
/// `cdz check` CLEAN; `cdz compile` SUCCEEDS; runs WRONG. This is the user-facing face of the still-live-
/// binding family (iters 27/28/34) — a `Map.insert` on a still-live env PARAMETER consumed in one operand
/// while a sibling SELF-RECURSIVE `ev` call reads the same env.
///
///   let x = 1 in (let x = 10 in x) + x       -- Cadenza source this interpreter models
///   should be (10) + (outer x = 1) = 11.  IT RETURNS 20  (the inner insert(env,"x",10) corrupts env, so
///   the outer `x` reads 10, giving 10 + 10).
///
/// SHARP (the family's recursive face, mapped iter 41):
///   • SHADOW (same key) is required: inserting a DIFFERENT key `y` while reading `x` is CORRECT
///     (`(let y=2 in y) + x` under {x:1} → 3) — only re-inserting the SAME key that a sibling later reads
///     corrupts, because `Map.insert` mutates that key's CHAMP slot in place;
///   • a SIBLING SELF-RECURSIVE `ev` call is required: `ev(insert(env,…), …) + ev(env, …)` where the
///     second `ev(env,…)` is a sibling self-call reading the un-inserted env. A NON-recursive helper does
///     the same correctly (`look(insert(env,x,99),x) + look(env,x)` → 100), and threading the insert INTO
///     the recursion (`ev(env,l) + ev(insert…, body)`) is correct — so a `let`-body that sees the new env
///     is fine; only a SIBLING reading the OLD env after the insert is wrong.
///
/// So it is the iter-27/28/29 root: `emit_call_args` (backend/wasm/select.rs) does not `dup` a borrowed
/// collection PARAM before a SELF-CALL whose callee consumes it — the caller-side dup an ordinary
/// `Core::Call` gets is omitted on the self-call arg path, so the consuming `map-insert` in the sibling
/// operand mutates the param the self-call then reads. (Reconciles iter-34's "params are safe" — true
/// WITHOUT a sibling self-call; a sibling self-call reading a just-consumed param is the miscompiling
/// shape.) Reproduces for List.push / Set.insert likewise.
///
/// This `main` is the interpreter evaluating `let x=1 in (let x=10 in x) + x`; it returns 20 (want 11).
type Ex =
  | Num(Int64)
  | Var(String)
  | Let(String, Ex, Ex)
  | Plus(Ex, Ex)

def ev(env: Map(String, Int64), e: Ex) = match e with
  | Ex.Num(n) => n
  | Ex.Var(x) => (match Map.lookup(env, x) with
    | Option.Some(v) => v
    | Option.None(_) => 0 - 1)
  | Ex.Let(x, rhs, body) => ev(Map.insert(env, x, ev(env, rhs)), body)
  | Ex.Plus(l, r) => ev(env, l) + ev(env, r)

/// `let x = 1 in (let x = 10 in x) + x` — should be 10 + 1 = 11; the shadow-insert corrupts env → 20.
def run() =
  ev(Map.empty,
    Ex.Let("x", Ex.Num(1),
      Ex.Plus(Ex.Let("x", Ex.Num(10), Ex.Var("x")), Ex.Var("x"))))

export { run }

